<title>UK: Rio Tinto continues copper studies in Spain.</title>
<headline>Rio Tinto continues copper studies in Spain.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Australian mining group Rio Tinto said on Wednesday its Spanish exploration unit would continue feasibility studies on the Las Cruces copper discovery in southern Spain.</p>
<p>The studies, which will take up to 24 months, will serve to determine whether the deposit can be economically mined.</p>
<p>The Las Cruces deposits are about 15 kilometres north of Seville. Exploration indicates the deposit consists of some 15 million tonnes of a resource of approximately six percent copper.</p>
<p>It also consists of more than one million tonnes of gold bearing (gossan) mineralisation containing about 6.5 grammes per tonnes.</p>
<p>Rio Tinto said the feasibility studies would focus on the higher grade copper and gossan resources present in the deposit.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
